<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pratap Singh Prabhakar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1740–1791</span> · Also known as Pratap Singh of Alwar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pratap Singh Prabhakar was a Naruka <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kachhwaha">Kachhwaha</a> chief who broke away from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaipur">Jaipur</a> in the 1770s and founded the state of Alwar in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>. He took the fort of Alwar in 1775 and expanded his lands with Mughal recognition. His successors made Alwar one of the main <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana">Rajputana</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pratap-singh-prabhakar.jpg" alt="Pratap Singh Prabhakar" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tpsn98290 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rao_Raja_Sri_Sawai_Pratap_Singh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
